WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:17.192
At beginning of summer vacation, everyone in town was talking about two things: the spectacular finale to the

2
00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:20.534
school's end-of-year recital and Muff Potter's trial.

3
00:00:21.695 --> 00:00:23.396
After his book had been torn, Mr.

4
00:00:23.416 --> 00:00:27.900
Dobbins became very quick-tempered, and he often used his whip on the children unjustly.

5
00:00:29.344 --> 00:00:32.106
Tom and the other schoolchildren had decided to get some revenge.

6
00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:34.868
Unknown to most of the town, Mr.

7
00:00:34.888 --> 00:00:35.809
Dobbins was bald.

8
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.431
He hid his baldness with a wig.

9
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:40.993
The plan was to expose Mr.

10
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.914
Dobbins' baldness to the whole town.

11
00:00:44.015 --> 00:00:46.317
Tom thought the plan was good, but not good enough.

12
00:00:47.538 --> 00:00:49.559
He felt it needed something extra special.

13
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.483
The night before the recital, Tom and several other boys slipped into the teacher's bedroom while he was

14
00:00:55.543 --> 00:01:01.538
sleeping. The boys knew that the teacher enjoyed several shots of whiskey before going to bed, and this

15
00:01:01.598 --> 00:01:02.718
made him a deep sleeper.

16
00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:05.079
The boys carefully painted Mr.

17
00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:06.680
Dobbins' bald head gold.

18
00:01:08.981 --> 00:01:10.902
The next evening Tom asked Huck to help.

19
00:01:11.642 --> 00:01:16.284
During the recital Huck cast his fishing line through the open window and snagged the teacher's wig.

20
00:01:17.465 --> 00:01:21.526
As the teacher was making his closing remarks, Huck reeled in his fishing line.

21
00:01:22.126 --> 00:01:25.428
The wig flew off, and the teacher's gold head was exposed.

22
00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.671
Everyone agreed it was a historic ending to the recital.

23
00:01:37.293 --> 00:01:40.475
The other event on everyone's mind was Muff Potter's trial.

24
00:01:41.295 --> 00:01:45.177
Whenever anyone mentioned it, or the murder, chills ran down Tom's spine.

25
00:01:46.218 --> 00:01:50.540
One day Tom went to Huck and asked, "Have you told anyone about what we saw?"

26
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.662
"Of course not," replied Huck.

27
00:01:53.682 --> 00:01:57.444
"Why, Tom, we wouldn't be alive two days if that got out.

28
00:01:58.492 --> 00:01:59.993
Injun Joe would kill us."

29
00:02:01.614 --> 00:02:02.475
Tom relaxed.

30
00:02:02.495 --> 00:02:05.737
"I guess we're safe as long as we keep quiet."

31
00:02:06.678 --> 00:02:11.061
The boys promised again that they wouldn't say anything to anyone about Doc Robinson's murder.

32
00:02:11.081 --> 00:02:14.183
"Muff Potter is going to die!"

33
00:02:14.604 --> 00:02:15.184
said Tom.

34
00:02:18.426 --> 00:02:20.468
"He is," replied Huck sadly.

35
00:02:20.488 --> 00:02:23.130
"Don't you feel sorry for him?"

36
00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:24.130
asked Tom.

37
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.132
"Yes," Huck said.

38
00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:29.534
"Muff may be a drunk, but he isn't a murderer.

39
00:02:30.514 --> 00:02:32.395
He's stood by me when I was out of luck."

40
00:02:33.836 --> 00:02:37.118
"He's fixed my kites plenty of times," added Tom.

41
00:02:37.138 --> 00:02:39.940
"I wish we could get him out of trouble."

42
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.063
"The only way to do that is to talk.

43
00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:47.985
But if we talk, we'll be dead," said Huck.

44
00:02:49.546 --> 00:02:52.088
Tom and Huck did the only thing they could do to help Muff.

45
00:02:53.088 --> 00:02:57.232
That was to pass tobacco, matches, and other things to Muff through the window of his cell.

46
00:02:58.293 --> 00:03:01.495
Muff was grateful, but the visits only made Tom more depressed.

47
00:03:04.218 --> 00:03:07.561
On the day of the trial, the whole town gathered in the courthouse to watch.

48
00:03:08.742 --> 00:03:14.246
The prosecution called many witnesses to the stand, and none of them said anything good about Muff Potter.

49
00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:20.352
Even Muff's lawyer didn't defend him, and the prosecution was able to quickly build a solid case against

50
00:03:20.412 --> 00:03:23.429
him. The judge decided to break early for lunch.

51
00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.052
Tom knew that Muff would be hanged if he didn't say anything.

52
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:32.474
He pulled Muff's lawyer aside as everyone was leaving the courtroom.

53
00:03:33.575 --> 00:03:36.076
Tom and the lawyer talked rapidly in hushed voices.

54
00:03:37.537 --> 00:03:42.660
When the trial resumed after lunch, the judge asked Muff Potter's lawyer if he had any witnesses that

55
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.520
he wanted to call.

56
00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:49.344
The lawyer looked at the judge and said, "Yes, I would like to call Thomas Sawyer to the

57
00:03:49.364 --> 00:03:53.906
stand." The courtroom buzzed like a hive of bees as everyone whispered.

58
00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.909
After the oath was administered, the lawyer asked Tom where he had been on the night of the

59
00:03:58.949 --> 00:04:03.572
murder. Tom was about to answer when he saw Injun Joe staring at him.

60
00:04:05.893 --> 00:04:09.775
Tom, suddenly afraid, stammered his answer.

61
00:04:09.795 --> 00:04:12.837
"I I was in the graveyard."

62
00:04:13.797 --> 00:04:17.960
Tom explained that he had been hiding behind the large tree near Hoss Williams' grave.

63
00:04:18.764 --> 00:04:22.767
The lawyer then showed the court the bag of Indian herbs that the boys had left behind.

64
00:04:24.508 --> 00:04:25.689
The courtroom was silent.

65
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.292
"How close were you to the murder that you witnessed?"

66
00:04:29.632 --> 00:04:30.853
the lawyer questioned Tom.

67
00:04:30.873 --> 00:04:35.596
"I was about as close as I am to you, sir," said Tom.

68
00:04:35.616 --> 00:04:39.319
"Can you describe to us exactly what you saw?

69
00:04:40.159 --> 00:04:43.742
Start at the beginning and don't leave anything out," cautioned the lawyer.

70
00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:46.504
Tom started his story.

71
00:04:47.584 --> 00:04:51.006
It was hard to speak at first, but soon words began to flow.

72
00:04:52.087 --> 00:04:58.590
He described Doc Robinson knocking out Muff with a rock and continued, "I saw Injun Joe grabbing a

73
00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:03.293
knife and—" Suddenly there was a loud crash.

74
00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:05.214
Injun Joe was gone.

75
00:05:06.415 --> 00:05:08.336
He had jumped through the courtroom window!
